import Qatlib.Concepts.LchsSimulation.TimeTrapezoid.LchsDefs

/-!
# LCHS compilation and resource identities

This module connects homogeneous and source branches of a finite LCHS discretization to prepared
circuit execution, in the setting of [AnLiuLin2023]. It proves coefficient-mass factorization,
branch unitarity, source loading identities, and explicit counts for amplification words and
their resource ledgers.

The cap-branch results identify the two-factor interaction picture propagator and the extra
factor in the printed three-factor expression. Taylor simulation counts and factorial cutoff
bounds complement the LCHS compilation estimates, following the truncated-series setting of
[BerryEtAl2015Taylor].

## Main statements

* `lchs2d_raw_vector`: recover the homogeneous contribution and source sum from loaded branches.
* `lchs2d_program_expanded`: identify the compiled run and its operation counts.
* `capTwoFactor_eq_propagator`: identify the corrected interaction picture factorization.
* `lchsHamT_native_query_rate`: bound queries at the native factorial cutoff.

## References

* [An, Liu, and Lin, 2023][AnLiuLin2023]
* [Berry et al., 2015][BerryEtAl2015Taylor]
* [Low and Wiebe, 2018][LowWiebe2018]
-/

